course: dictionary
lesson: 2055
title: Many meanings of one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word conscious can mean awake, knowing about something, done on purpose, or caring about something. The sentence around it tells you which meaning to use. «The nurse checked if the patient was conscious.» The nurse is asking whether the patient is awake and aware.
explain: «I'm conscious of the time, so I'll hurry.» Conscious of means you know about something or notice it. Ask yourself: does my meaning fit the sentence? Knowing that the time is getting late fits perfectly.
explain: «She made a conscious decision to save her pocket money.» A conscious decision is one made on purpose, not by accident. The word decision is a clue too. Words built from conscious, like «health-conscious», mean caring a lot about something.
explain: Maddie felt a bit self-conscious. Self-conscious means feeling shy or worried that other people are watching or judging you. Most people do not notice small things like a spot, but the self-conscious feeling makes it seem as if everyone can see it.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Conscious» means awake and aware of what is happening around you.
fact: «Conscious of» something means you know about it or notice it.
fact: A «conscious decision» is one you make on purpose.
fact: «Health-conscious» means caring a lot about your health, and «self-conscious» means feeling that other people are watching or judging you.
exercise: «The nurse checked whether the patient was conscious.» What does conscious mean here? | *Awake and aware of what is happening | Dressed in a smart uniform | Very quiet and calm | Sleeping soundly under a blanket
exercise: «I'm conscious of the time, so I must hurry.» What does conscious of mean? | Buying a new watch | Forgetting about the time | *Knowing about, or noticing, the time | Looking for a clock
exercise: «She made a conscious decision to save her pocket money.» What does conscious decision mean? | *A decision made on purpose | A decision made by accident | A decision someone else made for her | A decision made while asleep
test: Maddie felt a bit self-conscious. What does self-conscious mean here? | Cooking a meal alone | Feeling very proud of herself | *Feeling shy and worried that others are watching her | Being fully awake and alert
test: Ella is health-conscious. What does this suggest? | She has never been ill in her life | She dislikes all exercise | She is always asleep at night | *She cares a lot about eating well and staying fit
exam: «The doctor asked if the boy was fully conscious after his fall.» What does fully conscious most likely mean? | Badly hurt in his legs | Fully asleep and dreaming | *Completely awake and aware | Very angry about the fall
